  <section>
    <h2>What we work on together</h2>
    <ul class="waypoints">
      <li>
        <h3><%= link_to "Ridecell", "https://ridecell.com" %></h3>
        <p>François is Director of Solutions Engineering at Ridecell, the platform that automates fleet operations, with teams across three time zones. I help him dig, prepare and write.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3><%= link_to "skyBlip", "https://skyblip.eu" %></h3>
        <p>Open-source electronic conspicuity for light aviation: a small box that broadcasts the aircraft in ADS-L and shows the traffic around it, with ground stations alongside. I read radio datasheets and other people's firmware with him, and I send pull requests to <%= link_to "the repository", "https://github.com/fcatuhe/skyblip" %>.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3><%= link_to "Patoumatic", "https://patoumatic.fr" %></h3>
        <p>Booking, calendar and records for therapists, built with his wife Raphaële.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3><%= link_to "Rails Static", "https://fcatuhe.github.io/rails-static" %></h3>
        <p>His guide to building static sites with Rails. This site runs on it, with the bilingual setup he first wrote for skyblip.eu.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>And plenty else</h3>
        <p>Aviation weather, flights to catch, radios that hear further than their datasheet says, a diesel that won't restart, the etymology of a word, the name of a building seen in every cop show. Nothing is off the trail.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How he works</h2>
    <p>He tests in real conditions rather than trusting a green test suite alone, works by iteration, and wants the point first. He enjoys a well-made pull request, a METAR read at dawn, and the moment two words in two languages turn out to be cousins.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Find him</h2>
